{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.706 acc / 0.667 F1, outperforming config_018 (same but resnet50) by ~2.9% acc, establishing imagenet_vit_l as the stronger image encoder. Both experiments used avgpool aggregation, leaving the aggregation mechanism untested. Question: config_032 tests whether transformer aggregation (vs avgpool) further improves performance when paired with the stronger ViT-L encoder, while keeping all other settings identical to the current best. This is a clean single-variable change from config_005, isolating the effect of aggregation. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, reducing uncertainty about whether avgpool is a bottleneck for multimodal fusion is critical. Transformer aggregation is a more expressive way to combine multiprofile representations and could complement the attention-based ViT-L encoder. If it improves on 0.706, it opens a high-performing branch to further refine; if not, it confirms avgpool sufficiency and redirects budget toward RNA encoder or fusion strategy."
}

